7Z","email":"franck.nouama@gmail.com","name":"Franck Nouama"},"message":"feat: implement comprehensive security scanning and vulnerability detection (Issue #20)\n\nAdd complete security infrastructure with multi-layer vulnerability detection:\n\nSecurity Scanning Tools:\n- GitHub Actions security workflow with 9 specialized jobs\n- Dependency scanning for Go (gosec, nancy) and npm packages\n- Container security with Trivy for all microservices\n- Secret detection using TruffleHog and detect-secrets\n- SAST integration with CodeQL and SonarQube\n- OWASP dependency checking and license compliance\n\nPre-commit Security:\n- Comprehensive pre-commit hooks for proactive security\n- Custom scripts for credential and sensitive file detection\n- Security header validation for nginx configurations\n- ESLint security rules for JavaScript/TypeScript\n\nAutomated Security:\n- Dependabot configuration for all ecosystems (Go, npm, Docker)\n- Daily scheduled security scans at 2 AM UTC\n- Security report generation with multiple formats (SARIF, JSON, MD)\n- PR comments with security scan summaries\n\nSecurity Hardening:\n- Nginx security headers (X-Frame-Options, CSP, HSTS-ready)\n- Buffer overflow protection and timeout configurations\n- Comprehensive security documentation and incident response\n- GitHub security policy for vulnerability reporting\n\nConfiguration Files:\n- .github/workflows/security.yml - Main security scanning workflow\n- .github/dependabot.yml - Automated dependency updates\n- .pre-commit-config.yaml - Pre-commit security hooks\n- sonar-project.properties - SonarQube security rules\n- .secrets.baseline - Secret detection baseline\n- .eslintrc.security.json - JavaScript security linting\n- Scripts for security validation (3 files)\n- Complete security documentation (2 files)\n\nThe platform now implements enterprise-grade security scanning covering:\n- OWASP Top 10 compliance\n- CWE/SANS Top 25 protection\n- Automated vulnerability detection and remediation\n- 