ck.nouama@gmail.com","name":"Franck Nouama"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-13T22:34:04Z","email":"franck.nouama@gmail.com","name":"Franck Nouama"},"message":"feat: implement comprehensive unit tests for Order Service (Issue #11)\n\n- Domain layer tests: Complete Order aggregate testing with 100% coverage\n  * Order creation, validation, and business rules\n  * Item management (add, remove, update quantity)\n  * Status transitions and state machine validation\n  * Tax calculations and precision handling\n  * Type-specific operations (table ID, delivery address)\n\n- Application layer tests: Service orchestration with 46.9% coverage\n  * Order service operations with mocked dependencies\n  * Event publishing verification\n  * Error handling and edge cases\n  * Repository interaction patterns\n\n- Infrastructure layer tests: Repository serialization testing\n  * JSON marshaling/unmarshaling for complex nested structures\n  * Order status and type serialization\n  * Query parameter and filter serialization\n  * Data integrity validation\n\n- Interface layer tests: HTTP handler testing with 36.8% coverage\n  * Complete REST API endpoint coverage\n  * Request/response validation\n  * Error handling and status codes\n  * Mock service integration\n\nKey features tested:\n- Order lifecycle: CREATED → PAID → PREPARING → READY → COMPLETED\n- Business rule validation and status transition constraints\n- Tax calculation (10% rate) with floating point precision\n- Multi-type order support (DINE_IN, TAKEOUT, DELIVERY)\n- Event-driven architecture with domain events\n- Clean Architecture/Hexagonal Architecture patterns\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"750870096804e85a629f27c2fc87d3f1beceece3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francknouama/restaurant-platform/git/trees/750870096804e85a629f27c2fc87d3f1beceece3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francknouama/restaurant-plat